    "text": "An inductor <math> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>H</mtext></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </math> and a resistor <math> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>kΩ</mtext></mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </math> are connected in series to a battery of <math> <mn>15</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>V</mtext> </math> EMF in a circuit shown below. The key <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> has been kept closed for a long time. Then at <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is opened and key <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is closed simultaneously. At <math> <mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>ms</mtext> </math> , the current in the circuit will be : <math> <msup> <mi>e</mi> <mn>5</mn> </msup> <mo>≅</mo><mn>150</mn> </math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/P_52_Ques_A.jpg\" style=\"width: 208px; height: 167px;\" />",
